<p>Of course, there is a trade-off to be made, and in this case it’s primarily about disk space. Running psql’s <code>\\di+</code> and <code>\\dt+</code> commands we can see that the spatial-only index takes 1.9GB of storage, while the space-and-time index requires 2.7GB. This is a significant fraction of the size of the data itself: the <code>crimes</code> table is 5.5GB.</p>
